 "findings": {
  "low_level": [
   "The network is opt-W1's template recursion with the min and max exchange (T42) on the fp32 key twiddled to u32: 290 VIMNMX, 142 SHFL, 2 CREDUX.MIN, 16 VOTE, 30 POPC, 8 predicated STS in the N 128 k 16 latency kernel (two network copies), no BSSY, no BRA beyond the harness's five, 0 stack, 0 STL, 0 LDL in every warp cell (T36 check). Registers 30 to 64 in the latency kernel (W1_eager_same 24 to 59), 23 to 32 in the throughput kernel (40 at N 256 k 64), occupancy 8 blocks per SM (6 at N 256 k 64, same as the control). Level tile order (approaches/W1/warp_level_topk.cuh level_topk, all tiles sorted stage by stage at once, tile count halved per level) with the final merge truncated at stride k. Registers 30 to 64 in the latency kernel (identical to the eager form), throughput kernel 23 to 32 (40 at N 256 k 64)."
  ],
  "algorithmic": [
   "Against the eager order with the same recovery (N10_u32_trunc) in the same lock section, prefer_smaller_index latency: N 32 identical (504, 442), N 64 754, 706, 678 against 751, 696, 661 (schedule noise, the same dependency graph at two tiles), N 128 k 4, 16, 32 1013, 953, 918 against 1166, 1106, 1071 (0.87x, 13 percent), N 128 k 64 952 against 933, N 256 k 4, 16, 32 1480, 1422, 1386 against 2022, 1966, 1931 (0.73x, 27 percent), N 256 k 64 1435 against 1566 (0.92x). Throughput N 128 298 to 309 against 294 to 305 (plus 1.5 percent), N 256 k 4 to 32 276 to 280 against 286 to 291 (minus 4 percent), N 256 k 64 262 against 222 (plus 18 percent).",
   "Against the u64 word (W1_eager_same, through the control chain of the same session): N 128 k 16 953 against 1918 (0.50x), N 256 k 16 1422 against 3826 (0.37x)."
  ],
  "negative": [
   "No gain at one or two tiles (N 32, N 64): the eager and the level loop are the same dependency graph there and the level form measured 0 to 17 cycles slower. At N 256 k 4 to 32 the level order costs 4 percent throughput while saving 27 percent latency (the T 8 case where every tile is live during phase 1)."
  ],
  "surprises": [
   "With the two-class recovery the level order loses 4 percent throughput at N 256, with the one-ballot recovery of batch 2 it gains 23 percent in the same cells (N10_ge1_ltrunc 339 to 344 against N10_ge1_trunc 272 to 276): the throughput of these kernels is a schedule property, not a count property."
  ],
  "open_questions": [
   "Why the level order loses 2 percent at N 128 k 64 (M 2, two tiles: 952 against 933) when the dependency graph is the same, the T28 kind of swing."
  ]
 },
